-Pacing=on
+; How generated frames are presented. Both frames of a pair come from the
+; game's own Present; each is now shown for half a real-frame interval.
+; auto:        timed if that fits without lowering the game's frame rate,
+;              otherwise pipelined (Fix14 default).
+; low_latency: timed only: generated frame, then the real frame half an
+;              interval later; the wait shrinks if it would slow the game.
+; smooth:      pipelined only: the previous pair is shown with even spacing
+;              while the next pair is computed; one real frame more latency.
+; vblank:      Fix13 behaviour: both frames with VSync on consecutive
+;              refreshes (game held at half the refresh rate).
+; off:         both frames immediately (Fix12: uneven, generated frame is
+;              barely visible).
